The mechanism is simple: $\text{business pressure}
\longrightarrow
\text{exercise feels movable}
\longrightarrow
\text{stamina practice gets cut}.$ That is not a health formula. It is a founder-behavior pattern. The immediate obligation wins because its cost is visible now, while the cost of skipping exercise arrives more slowly.

