p.src:
The co-founder mechanism is concrete. One partner can step in when the other has a personal emergency. The two can also divide ordinary work before it becomes an emergency. In notation consistent with the energy chapter, if the solo founder has to absorb every demand, the load is concentrated: $L_{\mathrm{solo}}
=
L_{\mathrm{meetings}}
+
L_{\mathrm{decisions}}
+
L_{\mathrm{emergencies}}
+
L_{\mathrm{execution}}.$ A strong co-founder does not remove the load, but changes its distribution: $L_{\mathrm{founder\ A}}+L_{\mathrm{founder\ B}}
=
L_{\mathrm{company}}.$ The value is not arithmetic elegance. The value is redundancy. When the work can be redistributed, a personal interruption does not automatically become a company interruption.

